    <statement><p>The plane that passes through the point <m>\left(4,0,-4\right)</m> and is
perpendicular to both <m>5x-5y+3z = 22</m> and
<m>5y-2x-2z = -15</m> has
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/> as its implicit equation.</p>
</statement>
    <hint><B>Hint: </B>How do the normal vectors for two
perpendicular planes relate to each other?
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4y-5x+15z = -80</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
